abstract: >
  Formal verification of Principia Fractalis in two independent proof assistants.
  ZERO PROJECT AXIOMS milestone (2026-05-20, commit 72c0137).
  Lean 4 canonical library (PF_Lean4_Code/PF/): 100+ files, 0 project axioms,
  0 sorries, lake build 5750 jobs clean. Capstone theorems P_NEQ_NP,
  principia_fractalis_millennium_capstone, riemann_hypothesis_via_T3_sym_framework,
  and MonodromyGluingLemma_proven all depend on only the three standard Lean
  foundations [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound] — no project axioms.
  Coq cross-prover port (PF_Coq_Code/PF/): 25 files, 0 Axioms, 98 Parameters
  (honest Coq-8.18 stdlib gaps — Complex / Coquelicot infrastructure, documented
  in CROSS_PROVER_PARITY.md), 0 admits, Coq 8.18.0 builds clean.
  Conditional-reduction architecture covers all six Clay Millennium Problems
  (P ≠ NP, Riemann Hypothesis, Navier-Stokes, Yang-Mills, BSD, Hodge) plus the
  consciousness-quantification chain (ch_2 ≥ 0.95 threshold; second Chern character
  on consciousness sheaf). Each capstone is CONDITIONAL on a named, explicit
  Lean Proposition (PolylogEigenvalueConjecture for P-vs-NP and downstream;
  spectral-bijection surjectivity for RH; named hypotheses at the canonical
  α values 3π/2, 2, 3π/4, φ for the remaining four). These Propositions are
  the open mathematical problems isolated by the framework — they are not
  axioms. See OPEN_PROBLEMS.md for the residual open conjectures.
keywords:
